function packEntities(entities) {
  const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(entities.length);
  const view = new DataView(buffer);

  entities.forEach((entity, index) => {
    const id = entity.id & 0xF; // masking to get the 4 least significant bits
    const size = entity.size & 0x7; // masking to get the 3 least significant bits

    view.setUint8(index * (id + size), id);
    view.setUint8(index * (id + size) + 1, size);
  });

  return buffer;
}

function unpackEntities(buffer, length) {
  const entities = [];
  let index = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < length; i += 1 + Math.max(...entities.map(entity => entity.size))) {
    const id = buffer[index];
    const size = buffer[index + 1];

    entities.push({ id, size });
    index += 2 + size;
  }

  return entities;
}
```

In the `packEntities` function, we create an ArrayBuffer and a DataView to manipulate the buffer. We iterate through the entities and pack each one into the buffer. The id and size are masked to get the 4 and 3 least significant bits, respectively. The data is written to the buffer at an offset determined by the id and size.

In the `unpackEntities` function, we create an empty array to store the unpacked entities. We iterate through the buffer, unpacking each entity and pushing it into the array. The data is read from the buffer at an offset determined by the id and size of the previous entity. The function returns the array of unpacked entities.

