2. **Using `React.cloneElement`:**

`React.cloneElement` is used when you want to modify the existing children of a component. It creates a new React element with the same type as the old one, but with the new properties you specify.

```jsx
function MyComponent(props) {
  return (
    <div>
      {React.Children.map(props.children, (child, index) =>
        React.cloneElement(child, { key: index })
      )}
    </div>
  );
}

// Usage
